{% set name = "Universal Resolver" %}
{% set logo = "sketching" %}
{% set subtitle = "Community DID Infrastructure" %}
{% set repoTag = "" %}

{% extends "default.html.njk" %}
<!-- {% block svg %}

{% endblock %} -->

{% block content %}
  <section class="page-title theme-bg">
    <div class="container">
      <svg>
        <use xlink:href="/images/icons.svg#{{ logo }}"></use>
      </svg>
      <h1>{{ name }}</h1>
      {% if subtitle %}
        <h3>{{ subtitle }}</h3>
      {% else %}
        <h3>Decentralized Identity Foundation</h3>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="counter-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-md-center">
        <div class="col-6">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">A Successful Incubation</h2>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
              <i>As of October X, 2026, The Decentralized Identity Foundation is no longer hosting a "community staging 
              server" for the Universal Resolver. The complexity of hosting and administering it as a public resource has 
              grown over the years, and the number of commercial implementations of the Universal Resolver specification 
              (with free tiers) have largely obviated the need for DIF to "seed" the market, which is growing into 
              maturity.</i>
            </p>
            <p>
            Developers who were using DIF's community resolver (which was powered, all along, by GoDiddy's staging backend) 
            are encouraged to consider using one of the two commercial resolvers (with free-tiers) below. Both commercial 
            implementations are operated by DIF members, who maintain the respective reference implementations, including 
            ongoing review of new drivers. In historical order:
           </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<section class="counter-section gray-bg">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-md-center">
        <div class="col-3">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">GoDiddy, by DanubeTech</h2>
            <p>
              <i>Productionized reference implementation of the original Universal Resolver form-factor.</i>
            </p>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
            <a href="https://godiddy.com/app/resolve">GoDiddy's production front-end</a>, which continues to run DanubeTech's
             foundational reference implementation of the specification they 
             <a href="https://github.com/decentralized-identity/universal-resolver">donated to DIF</a> and managed here.
             It is comprised of a workhorse Java router and docker containers per method.
             </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-3">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">ThisDID, by GoPlausible</h2>
            <p>
              <i>Edge-worker-optimized and multi-backend version of the reference implementation for NPM-packaged drivers</i>
            </p>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
            They might also consider using <a href="https://thisdid.com">ThisDID.com</a>, a more recent productionization of the 
            <a href="https://github.com/decentralized-identity/did-resolver">TypeScript/NPM reference implementation</a>, which instead
             uses edge-worker to route and proxy resolution, and NPM packages per method. Both commercial implementations are 
             operated by DIF members, who maintain the respective reference implementations, including ongoing review of new 
             drivers.
             </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Blog End -->
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
  {{ super() }}
  <script src="/js/education.js"></script>
{% endblock %}